# TSan suppressions for the IV runner.
#
# The VENC VSI (struct venc_vsi, at the address INIT_DONE returns) is guest shared memory.  The
# daemon's guest threads write venc_vsi.list_free (plain 32-bit stores through n2a32_st32) and the
# AP thread reads the ring in n2ap_venc.c's ven_put_buffer().  On the phone those are coherent
# shared pages and the VCU protocol orders them with the IPI ack/done handshake; in the host model
# they are ordinary host-memory stores from another thread, so TSan must report that pair and no
# lock can remove it without changing the guest's code.  Suppress exactly that access pair; every
# other race in the runner (pthread shim, V40/V41 locks, guest log sink, DMA table) is expected to
# be absent and is not suppressed here.
race:ven_put_buffer
